.TH HEALTH-CHECK 1 "2025-12-20" "v1.1.0" "System Health Monitor"
.SH NAME
health-check \- Debian 12 system health analyzer and monitoring tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B health-check.sh
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B health-check
is a production-grade system health analysis script for Debian 12 hosts. It performs comprehensive monitoring of CPU, memory, disk, network, and service health, providing structured JSON output and human-readable reports with intelligent root cause analysis.

The script must be run as a non-root user with sudo privileges. It collects metrics from /proc, /sys, systemd, and system logs to provide a holistic health score (0-100) with component-level breakdowns.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress all output except exit code. Useful for cron jobs and automation.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Output JSON only (no markdown report). Ideal for machine parsing and monitoring systems.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Specify output format: \fBjson\fR, \fBmarkdown\fR, or \fBprometheus\fR. Default: markdown.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Write output to FILE instead of stdout. Creates parent directories if needed.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-monitor " " \fIINTERVAL\fR
Continuous monitoring mode. Run health check every INTERVAL seconds. Use with \-\-json for time-series logging.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-baseline " " \fIFILE\fR
Compare current metrics against baseline FILE. Highlights deviations and trends.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-score\-only
Output only the health score (0-100). Useful for quick checks and alerting thresholds.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-color
Disable colored output. Recommended for log files and non-terminal environments.
.TP
.BR \-\-debug
Enable debug logging. Shows detailed execution flow, timing, and intermediate values.
.TP
.BR \-\-check\-prerequisites
Run prerequisite checker only. Validates dependencies, sudo configuration, and directory permissions.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
System healthy (score >= 80). All checks passed without warnings.
.TP
.B 1
Warnings detected (score 50-79). System functional but requires attention.
.TP
.B 2
Critical issues (score < 50) or script execution error. Immediate action required.

.SH METRICS COLLECTED
.SS CPU Metrics
.IP \(bu 2
Load average (1min, 5min, 15min)
.IP \(bu 2
Per-core usage percentage
.IP \(bu 2
I/O wait percentage
.IP \(bu 2
CPU steal time (virtualization overhead)
.IP \(bu 2
Context switches per second

.SS Memory Metrics
.IP \(bu 2
Total, used, available RAM
.IP \(bu 2
Memory usage percentage
.IP \(bu 2
Swap usage (total, used, percentage)
.IP \(bu 2
Out-of-memory (OOM) event count
.IP \(bu 2
Top memory-consuming processes

.SS Disk Metrics
.IP \(bu 2
Filesystem usage per mount point
.IP \(bu 2
Inode usage percentage
.IP \(bu 2
I/O wait time
.IP \(bu 2
Read/write IOPS
.IP \(bu 2
Disk errors from kernel logs

.SS Network Metrics
.IP \(bu 2
Interface errors (RX/TX)
.IP \(bu 2
Dropped packets
.IP \(bu 2
Network throughput (bytes/sec)
.IP \(bu 2
TCP retransmit count
.IP \(bu 2
Established connections

.SS Service Metrics
.IP \(bu 2
Failed systemd units
.IP \(bu 2
Zombie/defunct processes
.IP \(bu 2
Processes in uninterruptible sleep (D state)
.IP \(bu 2
Service start failures (last 24h)

.SH ROOT CAUSE ANALYSIS
When the health score drops below 80, automatic root cause analysis is triggered. The RCA engine:
.IP \(bu 2
Detects recent package installations/upgrades (dpkg.log)
.IP \(bu 2
Identifies configuration file modifications
.IP \(bu 2
Tracks systemd service changes and restarts
.IP \(bu 2
Correlates timing of changes with score degradation
.IP \(bu 2
Provides actionable diagnosis and recommendations

.B Note:
RCA is advisory only. Correlation does not imply causation. Always validate findings manually.

.SH SCORING ALGORITHM
The overall health score (0-100) is calculated using weighted component scores:
.IP "CPU: 25%"
.IP "Memory: 30%"
.IP "Disk: 25%"
.IP "Services: 20%"

Each component score uses threshold-based evaluation:
.IP \(bu 2
< Warning threshold: 100 points
.IP \(bu 2
Warning to Critical: 100-50 (linear interpolation)
.IP \(bu 2
> Critical threshold: 50-0 (degraded scale)

.SH THRESHOLDS
Default alert thresholds (configurable in script):
.TP
.B CPU
Load: 70% warning, 90% critical (% of cores)
.br
I/O wait: 10% warning, 25% critical
.TP
.B Memory
Usage: 80% warning, 95% critical
.br
Swap: Any usage is warning, 50% critical
.TP
.B Disk
Usage: 80% warning, 90% critical (per filesystem)
.br
Inodes: 80% warning, 90% critical
.TP
.B Network
Errors: 100 warning, 1000 critical (per interface, 24h)
.TP
.B Services
Failed units: Any failure is critical

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/health-check/
Root cause analysis data directory. Stores historical scores, change logs, and RCA state.
.TP
.I /var/log/health.jsonl
Recommended log file for JSON output (append mode). Use with \-\-monitor for time-series data.
.TP
.I /etc/sudoers.d/health-check
Sudo configuration file. Required entries:
.br
.B username ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/dmesg, /usr/bin/journalctl

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B Basic health check
.EX
$ ./health-check.sh
.EE
Displays markdown report with all metrics and health score.

.TP
.B JSON output for monitoring
.EX
$ ./health-check.sh --json | jq '.score'
.EE
Extract health score for alerting threshold.

.TP
.B Continuous monitoring
.EX
$ ./health-check.sh --monitor 60 --json >> /var/log/health.jsonl
.EE
Run every 60 seconds, append JSON to log file.

.TP
.B Cron job (quiet mode)
.EX
*/5 * * * * /usr/local/bin/health-check.sh --quiet || /usr/local/bin/alert-team
.EE
Run every 5 minutes, alert on failure.

.TP
.B Prometheus export
.EX
$ ./health-check.sh --format prometheus > /var/lib/node_exporter/textfile_collector/health.prom
.EE
Generate Prometheus metrics for scraping.

.TP
.B Compare against baseline
.EX
$ ./health-check.sh --json > /etc/health-baseline.json
.br
$ ./health-check.sh --baseline /etc/health-baseline.json
.EE
Create baseline, then compare current state.

.TP
.B Check prerequisites
.EX
$ ./health-check.sh --check-prerequisites
.EE
Validate all dependencies and configuration before deployment.

.SH INTEGRATION
.SS Systemd Timer
.EX
# /etc/systemd/system/health-check.timer
[Unit]
Description=System Health Check Timer

[Timer]
OnBootSec=5min
OnUnitActiveSec=5min

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target

# /etc/systemd/system/health-check.service
[Unit]
Description=System Health Check

[Service]
Type=oneshot
User=monitor
ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/health-check.sh --json --output /var/log/health-latest.json
.EE

.SS Prometheus Alerting
.EX
groups:
  - name: health_check
    rules:
      - alert: SystemHealthCritical
        expr: system_health_score < 50
        for: 10m
        labels:
          severity: critical
        annotations:
          summary: "Critical health on {{ $labels.host }}"
.EE

.SS Slack Webhook
.EX
#!/bin/bash
output=$(./health-check.sh --json)
score=$(echo "$output" | jq -r '.score')
if [[ $score -lt 80 ]]; then
  curl -X POST $SLACK_WEBHOOK \\
    -d "{\\"text\\": \\"Health alert: $score/100\\"}"
fi
.EE

.SH SECURITY
.TP
.B Root Prevention
Script explicitly refuses execution as root (exit 2). Must run as non-root user with sudo.
.TP
.B Minimal Sudo
Only two commands require sudo: \fBdmesg\fR and \fBjournalctl\fR. All other metrics use /proc and /sys.
.TP
.B Input Sanitization
No user input is passed to sudo commands. All variables sanitized before shell expansion.
.TP
.B Temp File Security
Uses \fBmktemp\fR with restrictive permissions (600). Cleanup trap ensures deletion on exit.

.SH DEPENDENCIES
.SS Required
.IP \(bu 2
Bash 5.2+ (Debian 12 native)
.IP \(bu 2
jq (JSON processor)
.IP \(bu 2
bc (arbitrary precision calculator)
.IP \(bu 2
coreutils (df, free, uptime, nproc)

.SS Optional (graceful degradation)
.IP \(bu 2
sysstat (iostat for I/O metrics)
.IP \(bu 2
lsof (open files and connections)
.IP \(bu 2
net-tools (netstat for network stats)

.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.SS Script Not Running
.EX
# Check cron status
systemctl status cron
crontab -l | grep health-check

# Manual test
./health-check.sh --debug 2>&1 | tee /tmp/debug.log

# Check permissions
ls -la health-check.sh
ls -la /var/lib/health-check/
.EE

.SS Low Health Score
.EX
# Get detailed breakdown
./health-check.sh --json | jq '.alerts'

# Review RCA
./health-check.sh --json | jq '.root_cause_analysis'

# Component-specific check
./health-check.sh --json | jq '.metrics.cpu'
.EE

.SS High Execution Time
.EX
# Time individual components
time ./health-check.sh --debug 2>&1 | grep "Collecting"

# Check for hung commands
timeout 30 df -h
timeout 30 free -h
.EE

